# TypeAssert: BAS width subtyping accepts dict with extra fields
# Under BAS, [@[name: String] ...] accepts any record with AT LEAST name: String.
# Extra fields are allowed (width subtyping). No runtime E011 is raised.
# The [@Any ...] wrapper makes the type Unknown, which is consistent with the annotation.
[@[name: String] [@Any [name: "hello"  extra: "world"]]]
=== out
Dict({"name": String("hello"), "extra": String("world")})
